(footprint "R_LapPad_T50R0-250-12X"
	(version 20240108)
	(generator "aiee-librarian")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Vishay/Barry T50R0-250-12X, 50 ohm 250W BeO flanged RF termination. RESISTOR BODY IS OFF-BOARD, bolted to the user's external heatsink beside the PCB. THREE PADS: pad 1 = RF, the tab lap pad (3.048 x 0.127 mm silver-plated-copper tab laps onto this ONE SMD pad, sized 5.0 x 7.0 mm for a hand-solder lap overlap of ~4-6mm carrying 1.732 Arms continuous, 150W/50ohm CW - deliberately generous). Pad 2 (x2, west+east of pad 1, same net/number - same convention as this project's retired BFC280811339 footprint) = GND, the flange ground-bond lands: the resistor's cold end (flange) reaches PCB GND ONLY through two hand-soldered copper straps run from the flange top surface (1.575mm above the heatsink mounting plane) to these lands (2.635mm above the same plane, ~1.06mm of height over a short horizontal run across the mandatory 0.5mm flange-to-board gap) - see architecture/blocks.md B3 and state.json decision 'Adopt architect B3'. THE BOLTED FLANGE-TO-HEATSINK JOINT IS EXPLICITLY NOT RELIED ON AS AN ELECTRICAL PATH: on an anodised sink it is a 418pF/15.2ohm series capacitor at 25MHz (a ~10dB return loss, i.e. a dead board) plus a 15-25nH detour loop: it is a thermal/mechanical joint only. The two straps in parallel are the entire RF return, sized wide+short and placed symmetric about pad 1 specifically to keep that return-loop inductance low (~0.3nH pair, per blocks.md s2.3) and balanced. Pad 2 lands: 3.5 x 2.0mm each, centred +/-5.10mm off the pad-1/tab axis (blocks.md B3 specifies +/-4.75mm assuming a 4.4mm-wide pad 1; this footprint's pad 1 is actually 5.0mm wide, so the offset is widened by 0.35mm/side to hold blocks.md's own >=0.80mm HV clearance floor against the AS-BUILT pad 1 - see parts/T50R0-250-12X.json land_pattern.notes 2026-08-09 for the reconciliation) giving exactly 0.85mm copper-to-copper clearance to pad 1 (>= the board-wide 0.80mm HV floor, IPC-2221 A6 at 122.5 Vpeak). Mask and paste openings match pad copper 1:1 on all three pads (no additional expansion). The off-board mechanical envelope (flange 24.77x9.525mm, 2x Dia 3.302mm mounting holes 18.42mm apart on the flange centreline 3.175mm from each end, body block 9.525x9.525mm centred, tab exiting the middle of one 24.77mm side) is documented on User.Drawings ONLY, as a heatsink drilling template, INCLUDING the two strap-landing zones on the exposed flange top (outside the 9.525mm body block, centred at the same +/-5.10mm X as the PCB lands so each strap runs straight across the gap with no diagonal offset) - ORIGIN (0,0) = the point where the tab centreline crosses the board edge; local +Y = into the board, -Y = off-board toward the resistor/heatsink. The flange-to-board-edge GAP drawn there (1.0mm) is ILLUSTRATIVE ONLY - the true X-Y offset from the board edge is an outline/placement decision (architect's, not this footprint's). Courtyard is ON-BOARD ONLY (+0.25mm margin around all three pads), deliberately NOT wrapped around the off-board body: LEARNINGS 2026-07-22 - an off-board courtyard on a declared-edge part generates false placement-legality failures; keeping courtyard on-board avoids the argument entirely. Silk registration marks at the board edge show the flange/tab centreline (local X=0), the two bolt centrelines (local X=+/-9.21mm) and the two strap-landing centrelines (local X=+/-5.10mm) so a builder can align the physical straps to the lands and the flange. BeO SUBSTRATE HAZARD: beryllium oxide ceramic, sealed/covered element, safe under normal mounting - DO NOT machine, drill, grind or crush the resistor body (toxic dust).")
	(tags "RF termination flange lap-pad ground-strap off-board BeO heatsink")
